{title: Where He Leads Me}
{artist: E. W. Blandy / John S. Norris}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: F}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: where-he-leads-me.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Where_He_Leads_Me-Where_He_Leads_Me) and the Cyber Hymnal score (100% of syllables agree)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]I can hear my Savior [C7]calling,
[C7]I can hear my [F]Savior calling,
[F]I can hear my [Bb]Savior calling,
[Bb]Take thy cross and follow, [C7]follow [F]Me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Where He leads me I will [C7]follow,
[C7]Where He leads me [F]I will follow,
[F]Where He leads me [Bb]I will follow;
[Bb]I’ll go with Him, with Him, [C7]all the [F]way.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]I’ll go with Him through the [C7]garden,
[C7]I’ll go with Him [F]through the garden,
[F]I’ll go with Him [Bb]through the garden,
[Bb]I’ll go with Him, with Him [C7]all the [F]way.__[C7]__[F]__[Bb]__[C7]__[F]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]I’ll go with Him through the [C7]judgment,
[C7]I’ll go with Him [F]through the judgment,
[F]I’ll go with Him [Bb]through the judgment,
[Bb]I’ll go with Him, with Him [C7]all the [F]way.__[C7]__[F]__[Bb]__[C7]__[F]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]He will give me grace and [C7]glory,
[C7]He will give me [F]grace and glory,
[F]He will give me [Bb]grace and glory,
[Bb]And go with me, with me [C7]all the [F]way.__[C7]__[F]__[Bb]__[C7]__[F]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
